null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":38823,"output_tokens":1690,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Reconcile AC2/AC3 with the Testing 'derived-live, never-hardcoded' discipline: state whether the tests assert the literal counts (76/27) or assert the boolean/non-boolean partition invariant against a live-derived _SECTIONS scan.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["COH","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.131,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing: 'Census counts are derived LIVE from the tree, never hardcoded, following test_complexity_baseline.py's stated discipline.'","AC2: 'Verified by a test asserting its live count is 76.'","AC3: 'Verified by a test asserting its live count is 27.'"],"finding":"The Testing section states census counts are 'derived LIVE from the tree, never hardcoded,' yet AC2 and AC3 verify by 'asserting its live count is 76' and '27' — literal hardcoded expected values. It is unclear whether the tests derive the count independently and compare to the stored baseline, or assert against the literals 76/27.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f86fc049f685e767d","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section vs AC2/AC3","norm_id":"n5a919fcac8df8254","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A legitimately-added-and-excluded boolean key changes the live config_key count from 76 to 75; a test hardcoded to ==76 fails spuriously, while a live-derived test that only checks the partition invariant passes."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reframe AC2/AC3 to assert the partition property (config_key count + feature_flag count == total _SECTIONS entries, with feature_flag == count of boolean-coerced entries) derived live, rather than pinning literals 76/27; or explicitly state the counts are baseline-pinned snapshots and drop the 'never hardcoded' claim for these